<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1456" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">affector</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adf-</span></b> ), ātus, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>verb. dep.</i> [adficio]. *
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>To strive eagerly after</i> something: adfectatus
			est regnum, Varr. ap. <i><span class="en">Diom. p. 377</span></i>
			P.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> In later
			Lat., <i>to have an inclination for</i>, <i>to become attached to</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad mulierem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Herb. 15</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
